<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key><string>com.gascity.node-ghost-release</string>
  <!-- Node Ghost Release (2026-11-07, ga-moq226t): a bead in_progress owned by a Hetzner node alias (wa-worker-remote-N / ps-worker-remote-N, mark pilot.wa_node_alias)
       whose alias has NO live session for 15 min goes back to open/no owner, with a comment on the bead and ONE mail to the Mayor. One guarded write per bead, max 3 per sweep.
       LIVE (ga-yaoer2f, 07/11): NODE_GHOST_DRY_RUN=0 writes. It was shipped as 1 (logs WOULD-RELEASE, keeps its clock, writes nothing) and flipped only after the dry-run log
       showed real ghosts (wa-or1xlf: 91 min without a session, then re-dispatched by the Pilot; wa-7tufg6: session closed 22:09Z). Only an exact "0" writes; anything else is a dry run.
       KILL-SWITCH NODE_GHOST_ENABLED=0 or the file .gc/node-ghost-release.off. StartInterval 311, not 300: off the 300 s step the other daemons share, and still above one sweep
       (22-107 s measured over 46 sweeps at normal load, median 36 s; a round that outlasts the interval is not overlapped, the lock refuses a second copy). Registered in
       daemon-presence-watchdog.sh (DPW_CRITICAL + heartbeat on the .out, 900 s).
       CALL TIMEOUT (ga-pdyayy2, 08/11): NODE_GHOST_CALL_TIMEOUT=150 is the ceiling of each gc call (rig list, session list; mail send gets +20). The code default is 40, which was enough
       at normal load (44 of 46 rounds on 07/11); with the mini at load 26 the roster read took 58 s to over 90 s, hit the 40, and the round ended DEGRADED rc 1 with nothing decided,
       round after round, which the presence watchdog reads as CRASH-LOOP. Fail-closed stays: a read slower than 150 is still DEGRADED. A value that is not an integer, or is below 5,
       falls back to 40 without a word, so the start line of every round logs call_timeout=N: after a reload, that line (not this file) says what the job runs with. The selftest
       (section 13) pins this value against the measured latency and the StartInterval.
       NOT LOADED BY MERGING THIS FILE: ~/Library/LaunchAgents/ holds the live copy; reload it (launchctl bootstrap) after editing; see docs/runbooks/node-ghost-release.md. -->
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/usr/bin/python3</string>
    <string>/Users/athos/gt/.gascity-gastown-hq/scripts/node-ghost-release.py</string>
  </array>
  <key>WorkingDirectory</key><string>/Users/athos/gt/.gascity-gastown-hq</string>
  <key>StartInterval</key><integer>311</integer>
  <key>StandardOutPath</key><string>/Users/athos/gt/.gascity-gastown-hq/.gc/logs/node-ghost-release.out</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key><string>/Users/athos/gt/.gascity-gastown-hq/.gc/logs/node-ghost-release.err</string>
  <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
  <dict>
    <key>PATH</key><string>/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin:/Users/athos/go/bin:/Users/athos/.local/bin</string>
    <key>HOME</key><string>/Users/athos</string>
    <key>GC_CITY_PATH</key><string>/Users/athos/gt/.gascity-gastown-hq</string>
    <key>NODE_GHOST_ENABLED</key><string>1</string>
    <key>NODE_GHOST_DRY_RUN</key><string>0</string>
    <key>NODE_GHOST_CALL_TIMEOUT</key><string>150</string>
  </dict>
</dict>
</plist>
